    "result_text": "All done. The build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the acceptance test passes), and the audit log confirms the new format working end-to-end: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (region `NSW` + fiscal year `27` + `16E6609E` hash + Luhn check digit `1`).\n\n## Summary of changes\n\n**New unified `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`**, replacing the separate `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `checkDigit`.\n\n- **`MemberIdGenerator`** (renamed from `CustomerCodeGenerator`): `generate(postcode, registrationDate, telephone, lastName)` now assembles `region + 2-digit FY + HASH8 + Luhn(payload)`. The HASH8 (SHA-256 over `telephone+lastName`, first 8 upper-hex) is unchanged. `CHK = Luhn.checkDigit(region+FY+HASH8)` \u2014 `Luhn` already ignores the non-digit letters, so it operates purely on the digits as specified. `deduplicate` is kept generic (collision handling now applies to the memberId).\n- **`FiscalYear`**: extracted a `twoDigit(date)` helper for the FY segment and made `label` reuse it (no duplicated formatting).\n- **`Owner`**: `customer_code` column/field \u2192 `member_id` with `get/setMemberId`. Removed the now-redundant `getPrimaryIdentifier()` seam (unification is done; there's a single identifier).\n- **`OwnerMapper`**: dropped the `membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` mappings and their helper methods; `memberId` auto-maps like `customerCode` did. `resolveLocality` now derives the region from the postcode via `LocalityResolver` (the same source the memberId uses), instead of parsing the old `<REGION>-` prefix which no longer exists. Dropped the unused `Luhn` import.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`**: generates and dedups the memberId (passing `registrationDate` for the FY), checking `existsByMemberId`.\n- **Repositories** (`OwnerRepository`, Spring Data, JPA, JDBC): `existsByCustomerCode` \u2192 `existsByMemberId`, querying `member_id`.\n- **`OwnerCreatedEvent` / `OwnerAuditor`**: the audit record now references `memberId` (removed the `membershipNumber` field from the human-readable line).\n- **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres): `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id`, widened to `VARCHAR(32)` to accommodate the longer id (up to 18 chars, plus any collision suffix).\n- **`openapi.yml`**: replaced the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` schema properties with a single read-only `memberId`, and updated the `locality` description that referenced the old field.",
